<section class="why textured">
  <div class="container">
    <h2 class="section-title">Why repos-manager?</h2>
    <p class="subtitle">Your code lives on more forges and accounts than you can keep track of. repos-manager keeps a local, up-to-date copy of all of it, so you can work instead of hunting for repos.</p>

    <div class="pillars animate-stagger">
      <div class="pillar" style="--pillar:var(--accent)">
        <span class="pillar-icon"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"/><line x1="2" y1="12" x2="22" y2="12"/><path d="M12 2a15.3 15.3 0 0 1 4 10 15.3 15.3 0 0 1-4 10 15.3 15.3 0 0 1-4-10 15.3 15.3 0 0 1 4-10z"/></svg></span>
        <h3>Everything, in one command</h3>
        <p>Your own repos, your organizations and the projects you collaborate on, across every forge and account. One <code>sync --all</code>, no list of URLs to maintain.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="pillar" style="--pillar:var(--accent-green)">
        <span class="pillar-icon"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M12 22s8-4 8-10V5l-8-3-8 3v7c0 6 8 10 8 10z"/><polyline points="9 12 11 14 15 10"/></svg></span>
        <h3>Your work stays safe</h3>
        <p>These are the clones you work in. Updates are fast-forward only, local changes are never touched, and <code>status</code> tells you what is still unpushed.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="pillar" style="--pillar:var(--accent-purple)">
        <span class="pillar-icon"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><rect x="2" y="2" width="20" height="8" rx="2" ry="2"/><rect x="2" y="14" width="20" height="8" rx="2" ry="2"/><line x1="6" y1="6" x2="6.01" y2="6"/><line x1="6" y1="18" x2="6.01" y2="18"/></svg></span>
        <h3>Small forges welcome</h3>
        <p>GitHub and GitLab, but also Forgejo, Gitea, Bitbucket and Radicle, and as many self-hosted instances as you run, each in its own folder.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="compare animate">
      <h3 class="compare-title">How it compares</h3>
      <p class="compare-intro">Great tools already exist around Git repositories. Each one is built for a different job:</p>
      <table class="compare-table">
        <thead>
          <tr><th scope="col">Tool</th><th scope="col">What it does</th><th scope="col">Reach for it when</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr class="is-us">
            <th scope="row" data-label="Tool">repos-manager <span class="tag">this tool</span></th>
            <td data-label="What it does">Discovers every repository you can access on each forge, clones what is missing, fast-forwards the rest and reports what needs attention.</td>
            <td data-label="Reach for it when">You work across several forges or accounts and want all of it on disk, current, every day.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <th scope="row" data-label="Tool"><a href="https://github.com/x-motemen/ghq" rel="noopener">ghq</a></th>
            <td data-label="What it does">Clones repositories from their URL into a tidy, predictable directory tree.</td>
            <td data-label="Reach for it when">You clone projects one at a time and want them organized the same way.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <th scope="row" data-label="Tool"><a href="https://github.com/gabrie30/ghorg" rel="noopener">ghorg</a></th>
            <td data-label="What it does">Clones all the repositories of one organization or user in a single run.</td>
            <td data-label="Reach for it when">You need a whole organization locally, for onboarding, audits or searching through code.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <th scope="row" data-label="Tool"><a href="https://github.com/cooperspencer/gickup" rel="noopener">gickup</a></th>
            <td data-label="What it does">Backs repositories up and mirrors them to other hosts or storage.</td>
            <td data-label="Reach for it when">You want backups or mirrors of your repositories, typically on a schedule.</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
      <p class="compare-note">They are not mutually exclusive: back up with gickup, and keep working copies with repos-manager.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="quickstart" id="quickstart">
  <div class="container">
    <h2 class="section-title">Quick start</h2>
    <p class="subtitle">Installed with one of the commands <a href="#install">above</a>? Three commands and you are done.</p>

    <ol class="steps animate-stagger">
      <li class="step">
        <span class="step-num">1</span>
        <div class="step-body">
          <h3>Log in to your forges</h3>
          <p>Runs each installed provider CLI's login, or a single one with <code>repos-manager github login</code>.</p>
          <div class="step-cmd"><code><span class="prompt">$</span> repos-manager login</code><button class="copy-btn" data-copy="repos-manager login" aria-label="Copy command">Copy</button></div>
        </div>
      </li>
      <li class="step">
        <span class="step-num">2</span>
        <div class="step-body">
          <h3>Sync everything</h3>
          <p>Clones what is missing and updates the rest into <code>~/Documents/&lt;host&gt;/&lt;owner&gt;/&lt;repo&gt;</code>. Preview first with <code>--dry-run</code>.</p>
          <div class="step-cmd"><code><span class="prompt">$</span> repos-manager sync --all</code><button class="copy-btn" data-copy="repos-manager sync --all" aria-label="Copy command">Copy</button></div>
        </div>
      </li>
      <li class="step">
        <span class="step-num">3</span>
        <div class="step-body">
          <h3>Check what needs attention</h3>
          <p>Lists dirty, ahead, behind and diverged repos, so nothing stays unpushed.</p>
          <div class="step-cmd"><code><span class="prompt">$</span> repos-manager status</code><button class="copy-btn" data-copy="repos-manager status" aria-label="Copy command">Copy</button></div>
        </div>
      </li>
    </ol>

    <p class="quickstart-more">Next: <a href="/docs/configuration/">configure base directory and hosts</a>, <a href="/docs/filtering/">filter what gets synced</a>, or set up <a href="/docs/getting-started/">shell completions</a>.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<script>
(function() {
  // Reveal animations
  var targets = [];
  document.querySelectorAll('.animate').forEach(function(el) {
    el.classList.add('will-animate');
    targets.push(el);
  });
  document.querySelectorAll('.animate-stagger').forEach(function(parent) {
    Array.from(parent.children).forEach(function(child, i) {
      child.classList.add('will-animate');
      child.style.transitionDelay = (i * 0.08) + 's';
      targets.push(child);
    });
  });
  var observer = new IntersectionObserver(function(entries) {
    entries.forEach(function(entry) {
      if (entry.isIntersecting) {
        entry.target.classList.add('visible');
        observer.unobserve(entry.target);
      }
    });
  }, { threshold: 0 });
  targets.forEach(function(el) { observer.observe(el); });

  // Terminal demo. Each install tab has its own scenario; every line is
  // already in the page and all screens share one grid cell, so switching
  // or animating never changes the layout. Commands are typed into a span
  // while the rest stays invisible, which keeps line widths fixed.
  var demo = document.getElementById('terminal-demo');
  var titleEl = demo.querySelector('.terminal-title');
  var runId = 0;
  var pause = function(text) {
    if (!text) return 220;
    if (/^(Fetching|Scanning|Downloading|::|==>|Updating|Compiling|!)/.test(text)) return 900;
    if (/^(Done|Total|Finished)/.test(text)) return 700;
    return 380;
  };
  function play(name) {
    var run = ++runId;
    demo.dataset.theme = name;
    var screen = null;
    demo.querySelectorAll('.terminal-body').forEach(function(b) {
      var on = b.dataset.scenario === name;
      b.hidden = !on;
      if (on) screen = b;
    });
    titleEl.textContent = screen.dataset.title;
    // Fresh fake device code on every run, never a fixed one.
    screen.querySelectorAll('.otp').forEach(function(el) {
      var chars = 'ABCDEFGHJKLMNPQRSTUVWXYZ23456789', code = '';
      for (var k = 0; k < 8; k++) code += (k === 4 ? '-' : '') + chars.charAt(Math.floor(Math.random() * chars.length));
      el.textContent = code;
    });
    var lines = Array.prototype.slice.call(screen.querySelectorAll('.terminal-line'));
    lines.forEach(function(el) {
      el.classList.remove('shown', 'typing');
      var cmd = el.querySelector('.terminal-cmd');
      if (cmd) cmd.textContent = cmd.textContent;
    });
    var typeCommand = function(el, done) {
      var cmd = el.querySelector('.terminal-cmd');
      var text = cmd.textContent;
      cmd.innerHTML = '<span class="typed"></span><span class="caret"></span><span class="untyped"></span>';
      var typed = cmd.firstChild, rest = cmd.lastChild;
      rest.textContent = text;
      el.classList.add('shown', 'typing');
      var i = 0;
      (function next() {
        if (run !== runId) return;
        if (i >= text.length) { el.classList.remove('typing'); setTimeout(done, 600); return; }
        i++;
        typed.textContent = text.slice(0, i);
        rest.textContent = text.slice(i);
        // Long commands (pasted install one-liners) are typed faster.
        var fast = text.length > 40;
        var space = text.charAt(i - 1) === ' ';
        setTimeout(next, fast ? (space ? 60 : 12 + Math.random() * 22) : (space ? 90 + Math.random() * 120 : 35 + Math.random() * 70));
      })();
    };
    var index = 0;
    var step = function() {
      if (run !== runId || index >= lines.length) return;
      var el = lines[index++];
      if (el.querySelector('.terminal-cmd')) {
        typeCommand(el, step);
      } else {
        el.classList.add('shown');
        setTimeout(step, pause(el.textContent.trim()));
      }
    };
    setTimeout(step, 500);
  }

  // Install tabs drive both the command panel and the terminal scenario.
  var tabs = document.querySelectorAll('.install-tabs [role=tab]');
  tabs.forEach(function(t) {
    t.addEventListener('click', function() {
      if (t.getAttribute('aria-selected') === 'true') return;
      tabs.forEach(function(o) { o.setAttribute('aria-selected', o === t ? 'true' : 'false'); });
      document.querySelectorAll('.install-panel').forEach(function(p) { p.hidden = p.dataset.panel !== t.dataset.tab; });
      play(t.dataset.tab);
    });
  });
  play(document.documentElement.dataset.os === 'windows' ? 'windows' : 'unix');

  // Copy buttons
  function toast(text) {
    var t = document.createElement('div');
    t.className = 'copy-toast visible';
    t.textContent = text;
    document.body.appendChild(t);
    setTimeout(function() { t.classList.remove('visible'); }, 1800);
    setTimeout(function() { t.remove(); }, 2100);
  }
  function fallbackCopy(text) {
    var ta = document.createElement('textarea');
    ta.value = text;
    ta.style.cssText = 'position:fixed;opacity:0';
    document.body.appendChild(ta);
    ta.select();
    document.execCommand('copy');
    ta.remove();
  }
  document.querySelectorAll('.copy-btn').forEach(function(btn) {
    btn.addEventListener('click', function() {
      var text = btn.dataset.copy;
      var done = function() {
        btn.textContent = 'Copied';
        btn.classList.add('copied');
        setTimeout(function() { btn.textContent = 'Copy'; btn.classList.remove('copied'); }, 1500);
        toast('Copied to clipboard');
      };
      if (navigator.clipboard && window.isSecureContext) {
        navigator.clipboard.writeText(text).then(done, function() { fallbackCopy(text); done(); });
      } else {
        fallbackCopy(text);
        done();
      }
    });
  });
})();
</script>
